research/audit/wave12-proof-contracts.json-10333-          "source_section": "Definition",
research/audit/wave12-proof-contracts.json-10334-          "quote": "Let $X$ be a set and let $f_k:X\\to\\mathbb{R}$ for $k\\in\\mathbb{N}$. The **series of real-valued functions** $\\sum f_k$ is studied through its partial-sum functions $$S_n(x):=\\sum_{k<n}f_k(x)\\qquad(n\\in\\mathbb{N},\\ x\\in X),$$ where the sum on the right is the finite sum of [[def-series]]. Thus $S_0$ is the zero function and $S_{n+1}=S_n+f_n$ under the pointwise operations of [[def-function-space]]. The series $\\sum f_k$ **converges pointwise** to $S:X\\to\\mathbb{R}$ when $S_n\\to S$ pointwise, and it **converges uniformly** to $S$ when $S_n\\to S$ uniformly ([[def-pointwise-uniform-and-uniformly-cauchy-convergence]]). The series is **absolutely convergent at $x\\in X$** when the scalar series $\\sum |f_k(x)|$ converges. It is **absolutely pointwise convergent** when this holds for every $x\\in X$.",
research/audit/wave12-proof-contracts.json-10335-          "quote_selection": "full-source-section",
research/audit/wave12-proof-contracts.json-10336-          "uses": [
