research/audit/wave12-certifier-tasks/a6-cor-uniform-cauchy-criterion-function-series.md-117-**Given:** A set $X$, functions $f_k:X\to\mathbb{R}$, and partial-sum functions $S_r(x)=\sum_{k<r}f_k(x)$.
research/audit/wave12-certifier-tasks/a6-cor-uniform-cauchy-criterion-function-series.md-118-
research/audit/wave12-certifier-tasks/a6-cor-uniform-cauchy-criterion-function-series.md:119:[L1] The series $\sum f_k$ converges uniformly exactly when its partial-sum sequence $(S_r)$ converges uniformly ([[def-series-of-real-functions]]).
research/audit/wave12-certifier-tasks/a6-cor-uniform-cauchy-criterion-function-series.md-120-
research/audit/wave12-certifier-tasks/a6-cor-uniform-cauchy-criterion-function-series.md-121-[L2] A sequence of real-valued functions converges uniformly exactly when it is uniformly Cauchy ([[thm-uniform-cauchy-criterion-real-functions]]).
research/audit/wave12-certifier-tasks/a6-cor-uniform-cauchy-criterion-function-series.md-122-
research/audit/wave12-certifier-tasks/a6-cor-uniform-cauchy-criterion-function-series.md:123:[L3] For $n>m$, $\sum_{k=m+1}^{n}f_k(x)=S_{n+1}(x)-S_{m+1}(x)$, and $|-u|=|u|$ for every real $u$ ([[def-series-of-real-functions]], [[lem-of-abs-value]]).
