research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/thm-weierstrass-m-test-for-function-series.md-55-
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/thm-weierstrass-m-test-for-function-series.md-56-[L2] A convergent real series has uniformly small scalar tails: for every real $\varepsilon>0$ there is $N$ such that $\left|\sum_{k=m+1}^{n}a_k\right|<\varepsilon$ whenever $n>m\ge N$ ([[thm-series-cauchy-criterion]]).
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/thm-weierstrass-m-test-for-function-series.md-57-
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/thm-weierstrass-m-test-for-function-series.md-58-[L3] Repeated triangle inequalities for finite sums give $\left|\sum_{k=p}^{q}u_k\right|\le\sum_{k=p}^{q}|u_k|$, and finite sums preserve termwise inequalities ([[lem-of-triangle-inequality]], [[lem-of-abs-value]], [[def-finite-sum]], [[lem-finite-sum-laws]]).
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/thm-weierstrass-m-test-for-function-series.md-59-
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/thm-weierstrass-m-test-for-function-series.md:60:[L4] A function series converges uniformly exactly when its tails are uniformly small ([[cor-uniform-cauchy-criterion-function-series]], [[def-series-of-real-functions]]).
