research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/thm-weierstrass-m-test-for-function-series.md-429-**Given:** A set $X$, functions $f_k:X\to\mathbb{R}$, and partial-sum functions $S_r(x)=\sum_{k<r}f_k(x)$.
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/thm-weierstrass-m-test-for-function-series.md-430-
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/thm-weierstrass-m-test-for-function-series.md:431:[L1] The series $\sum f_k$ converges uniformly exactly when its partial-sum sequence $(S_r)$ converges uniformly ([[def-series-of-real-functions]]).
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/thm-weierstrass-m-test-for-function-series.md-432-
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/thm-weierstrass-m-test-for-function-series.md-433-[L2] A sequence of real-valued functions converges uniformly exactly when it is uniformly Cauchy ([[thm-uniform-cauchy-criterion-real-functions]]).
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/thm-weierstrass-m-test-for-function-series.md-434-
