research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-8018-research/audit/wave5-topology-function-spaces.provenance.jsonl-19-{"id": "def-equicontinuity", "statement": "literature-derived", "proof": "not-applicable", "evidence": "exact-source", "urls": ["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Equicontinuity", "https://faculty.etsu.edu/gardnerr/5357/notes/Munkres-45.pdf"], "rationale": "All three notions are sourced verbatim in the item's own metric epsilon-delta form. Wikipedia, Equicontinuity: 'The family F is equicontinuous at a point x_0 in X if for every epsilon > 0, there exists a delta > 0 such that d(f(x_0), f(x)) < epsilon for all f in F and all x such that d(x_0, x) < delta'; and 'The family F is uniformly equicontinuous if for every epsilon > 0, there exists a delta > 0 such that d(f(x_1), f(x_2)) < epsilon for all f in F and all x_1, x_2 in X such that d(x_1,x_2) < delta.' Munkres Sec. 45 gives pointwise boundedness verbatim: 'a subset F of C(X,Y) is pointwise bounded under d if for each a in X, the subset F_a = {f(a) | f in F} of Y is bounded under d.' No hypothesis, quantifier or direction changed. Definition, no proof component.", "alpha_concurred": false, "at": "2026-08-05"}
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-8019-research/audit/wave5-topology-function-spaces.provenance.jsonl:20:{"id": "thm-dini", "statement": "ai-altered", "proof": "ai-generated", "evidence": "semantic-source", "urls": ["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dini%27s_theorem", "https://faculty.etsu.edu/gardnerr/5357/notes/Munkres-45.pdf"], "rationale": "Sourced statement: X a compact TOPOLOGICAL space, (f_n) a monotonically increasing sequence of continuous real-valued functions converging pointwise to a continuous f : X -> R; then the convergence is uniform, and the monotonically decreasing form holds too. The item is that statement with X specialised to a compact METRIC space, the monotonicity written out pointwise as f_k(x) <= f_{k+1}(x), and the nonincreasing form recorded as a consequence of applying the theorem to the negatives rather than proved separately. Added hypothesis and reformulation only; conclusion and direction unchanged. Local proof, kept choice-free by taking the finite subcover as a list of indices.", "alpha_concurred": false, "at": "2026-08-05"}
--
